From: omarchy-m5 local integration
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: T6050 N1 device-tree hand-off for the kernel-owned train

Fill the hand-off DT for Linux's apple,t6050-pcie host and the protocol-27
Centauri drivers on J714s: the N1 control identity (firmware-name,
platform-id, protocol), the six host tunable lists and the pci-bridge0 port
lists from this boot's ADT, and the root port plus its DART enabled together
only when the DT lets Linux power and train the link (pwren-gpios and
apple,manual-availability).

Adapted from omacom/m1n1 src/kboot_n1.c at 02785a35e046 (MIT) with the J714s
host-list admission from TripleU613's installer loader, after
rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux m1n1 patch 0028. Unlike those, this version
performs no MMIO and never trains a link in the loader: any missing or
unusable input leaves the port and DART disabled and Linux boots without
the N1. A DT whose PCIe host is disabled is not modified.

Apply after patches/m1n1-gpu 0001 and 0002. Offline harness:
patches/m1n1-gpu/smoke-n1.py.
---
